message.content:
{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2184-10-02 12:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I’ll be helping take care of you during this hospital stay. You came in with nausea and vomiting, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2184-10-02 12:19:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, that’s right. It’s been going on for about 10 days. Feels just like my past blockages—tightness and pressure all over, especially upper left and right."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2184-10-02 12:20:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. And you’ve had similar episodes before with your mesenteric fibromatosis. You mentioned the pain didn’t get better with your usual morphine suppository?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2184-10-02 12:21:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, not really. I took it, but the pain stayed strong. I only vomited once this morning, but the nausea is constant."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2184-10-02 12:22:05",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay. We’ve started your TPN through your femoral line, and you’ll stay on IV fluids. We’ll hold off on food for now—NPO—to let your gut rest."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2184-10-02 12:23:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s fine. I’ve done this before. But can we do something for the nausea? The IV Phenergan helps a little."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2184-10-02 12:24:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re giving IV Phenergan now, but we’ll also try a rectal suppository later to see if that works better for you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2184-10-02 12:25:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, thanks. My last bowel movement was this morning—loose and pencil-thin, like always during a flare."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2184-10-02 12:26:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, and you’re still passing gas, just less than usual. That’s consistent with your history. We’ve ordered an abdominal X-ray to check for obstruction."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2184-10-02 12:27:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the X-ray won’t show a blockage? Because it feels like one."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2184-10-02 13:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The X-ray came back. It shows a nonspecific bowel gas pattern—no clear sign of obstruction. There’s stool and air in the rectum, but nothing blocked higher up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2184-10-02 13:31:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Huh. So why do I feel this way if there’s no blockage?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2184-10-02 13:32:40",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your pain and nausea are likely due to your chronic motility issues and fibromatosis flare. Even without a physical blockage, your gut can act like it’s obstructed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2184-10-02 13:34:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Ah, okay. So we treat it like past flares?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2184-10-02 13:35:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. We’ll continue IV fluids, use IV Dilaudid for breakthrough pain, and keep the morphine suppositories. We’ll also add glycerin suppositories to help move things along."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2184-10-03 09:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. How’s the nausea today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2184-10-03 09:16:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "A little better. The rectal Phenergan seemed stronger than the IV. Can I keep using that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2184-10-03 09:17:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ll switch to PR Phenergan as needed. We’re also going to try advancing you to clear liquids later if you’re still doing well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2184-10-03 09:18:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. I’ve been on TPN for so long, I miss tasting things."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2184-10-03 09:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll go slow. If you tolerate clear liquids, we can gradually build up. But if you start vomiting again, we’ll go back to NPO."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2184-10-04 10:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve been on clear liquids since yesterday. How’s your stomach holding up?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2184-10-04 10:06:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Pretty good! No vomiting. I’d like to try a soft food—maybe applesauce or broth?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2184-10-04 10:07:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We can add those. But let’s hold off on a full regular diet for now. We don’t want to trigger another episode."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2184-10-05 08:45:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Doctor, I tried a regular meal last night—just mashed potatoes and chicken—and I threw up twice."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2184-10-05 08:46:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I’m sorry to hear that. We’ll switch you back to clear liquids. Your GI doctor agreed—better to go slow. You can start advancing again at home when you’re stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2184-10-05 08:48:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That makes sense. It’s frustrating, but I don’t want to be back here next week."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2184-10-05 08:49:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll give you a prescription for rectal Phenergan to use at home so you can manage nausea early."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2184-10-06 09:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your labs are stable. Hemoglobin is 10.6, which is better than your baseline. No signs of infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2184-10-06 09:21:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. And my femoral line—infusions have been burning a bit the last day or two."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2184-10-06 09:22:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I noticed mild redness. We’re going to do a line study tomorrow to check for a leak or tear. You’ll need contrast, so we’ll pre-treat with prednisone since you’ve had reactions before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2184-10-06 09:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I get hives with iodine. So this is just a scan to check the line, not surgery?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2184-10-06 09:25:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. It’s a fluoroscopy. If there’s a small tear, they can often repair it during the same procedure."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2184-10-07 10:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re scheduling the line study for tomorrow morning. You’ll get 50 mg prednisone tonight and again tomorrow, 3 and 1 hour before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2184-10-07 10:16:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And my Lupron injection—is it due soon?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2184-10-07 10:17:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You had your last one about three weeks ago, so yes, we’ll give you your monthly Lupron while you’re here."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2184-10-07 10:19:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I don’t want the fibromatosis to flare more."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2184-10-08 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The line study is done. There was a small tear near the hub of the red lumen, but they repaired it successfully. No leak in the tunneled part."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2184-10-08 14:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s fixed? No replacement needed?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2184-10-08 14:02:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Correct. The catheter itself is intact. We’ll continue using it for TPN. You’ll need to do daily ethanol locks to prevent infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2184-10-08 14:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I remember—2 mL per lumen, not for IV use. Got it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2184-10-09 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve been on clear liquids for two days with no vomiting. How’s your pain and nausea?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2184-10-09 09:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Much better. Pain is mild, maybe a 3. I’ve been using the morphine suppository once a day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2184-10-09 09:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great. We’ll keep your pain meds as is. At discharge, we’re increasing the morphine suppository to 20 mg every 6 hours as needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2184-10-09 09:03:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s higher than before. Is that safe?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2184-10-09 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, it’s within your usual range. You’ve needed more during flares, and we want you to have enough at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2184-10-09 09:06:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, good. And I’ll keep using the rectal Phenergan as needed?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2184-10-09 09:07:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, 25 mg every 6 hours if nauseated. We’re adding that to your discharge meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2184-10-10 10:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing really well. We’re planning to discharge you tomorrow morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2184-10-10 10:31:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great! What do I need to do at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2184-10-10 10:32:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Resume your home TPN through the femoral line. Stay on clear liquids for a few days, then slowly add soft foods as tolerated."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2184-10-10 10:33:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my other meds—everything else stays the same?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2184-10-10 10:35:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, all your regular meds continue—Lupron, levothyroxine, gabapentin, and the rest. We’re just adjusting the pain and nausea meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2184-10-10 10:36:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And follow-up with my GI doctor?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2184-10-10 10:37:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, please follow up with Dr. ___ in one week. Call sooner if you have severe pain, vomiting, or redness at the line site."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2184-10-10 10:38:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. I feel a lot better than when I came in."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2184-10-11 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your discharge orders are ready. You’re cleared to go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2184-10-11 08:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I’m ready to get back to my routine."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2184-10-11 08:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well—abdomen soft, pain controlled, no nausea. Keep using the ethanol lock daily on your line."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2184-10-11 08:03:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll do that. And I’ll start advancing my diet slowly, like we talked about."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2184-10-11 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. Take care, and don’t hesitate to call your team if anything changes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2184-10-11 08:06:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thanks for everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2184-10-11 08:07:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Have a safe trip home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2184-10-11 08:08:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m glad the X-ray didn’t show a blockage. That was worrying me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2184-10-11 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, it’s reassuring. Your symptoms were due to your chronic condition, not a new obstruction. That’s why the conservative approach worked."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2184-10-11 08:11:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my migraines—they’ve been okay, just baseline."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2184-10-11 08:12:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we treated them as needed with sumatriptan and butorphanol. No new neuro issues."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2184-10-11 08:13:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I was worried the pain meds might trigger more headaches."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 68,
      "time": "2184-10-11 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We monitored that closely. You’re on the same regimen as before, so it shouldn’t be an issue."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 69,
      "time": "2184-10-11 08:16:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my hemoglobin—is it okay that it’s 10.6?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 70,
      "time": "2184-10-11 08:17:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, for you, that’s actually good—better than your usual 25% hematocrit. No need for iron infusion this time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 71,
      "time": "2184-10-11 08:18:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. I don’t miss those IV treatments."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 72,
      "time": "2184-10-11 08:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll keep you on oral ferrous sulfate. Stay consistent with it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 73,
      "time": "2184-10-11 08:21:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. And my constipation—I’ve been using senna and Miralax."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 74,
      "time": "2184-10-11 08:22:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, keep that up. We’re discharging you with both to prevent backup."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 75,
      "time": "2184-10-11 08:23:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve learned—better to stay ahead of it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 76,
      "time": "2184-10-11 08:25:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Smart approach. You know your body best."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 77,
      "time": "2184-10-11 08:26:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "One last thing—my asthma. I used my inhaler a couple times."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 78,
      "time": "2184-10-11 08:27:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we had albuterol available. Your lungs sounded clear. Just keep using it as needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 79,
      "time": "2184-10-11 08:28:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will do. I think that’s everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 80,
      "time": "2184-10-11 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, you’re all set. Discharge paperwork is ready. Take care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 81,
      "time": "2184-10-11 08:31:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor. I appreciate all your help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 82,
      "time": "2184-10-11 08:32:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re very welcome. Get some rest at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 83,
      "time": "2184-10-11 08:33:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. And I’ll call if anything comes up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 84,
      "time": "2184-10-11 08:35:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. We’re here if you need us."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 85,
      "time": "2184-10-11 08:36:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks again. I’m ready to go."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2184-10-02 12:18:00",
    "admission_end": "2184-10-11 12:24:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with a long history of mesenteric fibromatosis and recurrent small bowel obstructions was admitted for nausea, vomiting, and abdominal pain consistent with prior flares. Imaging showed no mechanical obstruction, and symptoms were managed with NPO status, TPN, IV fluids, and pain and nausea control using IV Dilaudid and rectal morphine and Phenergan. She was advanced to clear liquids but redeveloped vomiting after attempting a regular diet, prompting reversion to clear liquids at discharge with instructions to advance slowly at home. A tear in the femoral TPN line hub was repaired via nonoperative intervention, and ethanol locks were initiated. Her chronic conditions, including migraines, hypothyroidism, anemia of chronic disease, and asthma, remained stable. She was discharged home on a clear liquid diet with updated PR medications for pain and nausea, instructions to resume TPN, and plans for outpatient follow-up.",
    "problems": [
      "Neoplasm of uncertain behavior of connective and other soft tissue",
      "Unspecified intestinal obstruction",
      "Mechanical complication of other vascular device, implant, and graft",
      "Other constipation",
      "Gastrostomy status",
      "Migraine, unspecified, without mention of intractable migraine without mention of status migrainosus",
      "Asthma, unspecified type, unspecified",
      "Anemia of other chronic disease",
      "Unspecified acquired hypothyroidism",
      "Chronic hepatitis C without mention of hepatic coma",
      "Methicillin susceptible Staphylococcus aureus in conditions classified elsewhere and of unspecified site",
      "Other specified procedures as the cause of abnormal reaction of patient, or of later complication, without mention of misadventure at time of procedure"
    ]
  }
}
